WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.039 --> 00:00:17.401
Redbeard was hanging around outside your house?"

2
00:00:17.781 --> 00:00:18.902
Henry asked William.

3
00:00:18.922 --> 00:00:21.724
"Why?" "I don't know.

4
00:00:22.165 --> 00:00:23.526
I only saw him for a second."

5
00:00:24.227 --> 00:00:25.187
William looked around.

6
00:00:25.207 --> 00:00:27.589
"Hey, where's everybody else?"

7
00:00:27.609 --> 00:00:29.511
"I think they're over there."

8
00:00:29.831 --> 00:00:30.472
Cole pointed.

9
00:00:31.644 --> 00:00:33.646
William took a few steps and then paused.

10
00:00:33.666 --> 00:00:35.348
"Aren't you guys coming?"

11
00:00:35.368 --> 00:00:38.390
"We'll be there in a minute," Henry said.

12
00:00:39.531 --> 00:00:41.173
After William left, Cole shrugged.

13
00:00:41.193 --> 00:00:43.114
"That's weird," he said.

14
00:00:43.134 --> 00:00:46.177
"Why is Roger hanging around William's house?

15
00:00:46.838 --> 00:00:48.019
Is he looking for more booty?"

16
00:00:48.039 --> 00:00:52.062
"Maybe." Henry glanced at the general store.

17
00:00:52.082 --> 00:00:58.088
"Come on, let's go inside and ask if Roger was really here earlier.

18
00:00:59.312 --> 00:01:02.513
Maybe he found that cup on the beach and used it for his alibi."

19
00:01:05.975 --> 00:01:08.216
Henry and Cole hurried into the general store.

20
00:01:08.876 --> 00:01:10.617
A woman was behind the cash register.

21
00:01:11.577 --> 00:01:14.759
She had a friendly smile and hair the same color as Anna's.

22
00:01:14.779 --> 00:01:18.280
"Hello, boys," she greeted them.

23
00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:20.721
"I haven't seen you around here before.

24
00:01:20.741 --> 00:01:23.443
Are you William's new friends from Belltown?"

25
00:01:24.323 --> 00:01:26.444
Henry guessed that the woman was Anna's mother.

26
00:01:27.324 --> 00:01:29.945
He also guessed that Anna had told her about their visit.

27
00:01:30.565 --> 00:01:32.365
"Yes, we are," he told her.

28
00:01:32.385 --> 00:01:36.006
"Welcome to Sea Cove," Anna's mother said.

29
00:01:36.026 --> 00:01:38.687
"I hope you're enjoying the treasure hunt."

30
00:01:38.707 --> 00:01:41.108
"It's great," Cole said.

31
00:01:41.128 --> 00:01:44.729
"We were wondering something," Henry added.

32
00:01:44.749 --> 00:01:49.370
"Did a man named Roger Redbeard come in here a little while ago?"

33
00:01:50.430 --> 00:01:52.551
"Roger?" Anna's mom smiled.

34
00:01:52.571 --> 00:01:53.951
"Why yes.

35
00:01:54.451 --> 00:01:56.652
He did come in earlier today."

36
00:01:57.812 --> 00:02:00.174
Just then another customer came toward the register.

37
00:02:01.094 --> 00:02:02.916
Henry and Cole stepped away to talk.

38
00:02:05.057 --> 00:02:08.359
"I guess Roger does have a good alibi after all," Cole said.

39
00:02:08.379 --> 00:02:12.062
"If he was here earlier, he couldn't have taken those tickets."

40
00:02:12.902 --> 00:02:15.384
"Yeah." Henry bit his lip.

41
00:02:16.044 --> 00:02:19.506
If Roger hadn't done it, that meant one of their friends was the thief.

42
00:02:19.526 --> 00:02:21.067
"Let's go."

43
00:02:21.088 --> 00:02:22.989
"Hold on."

44
00:02:23.609 --> 00:02:24.730
Cole stepped toward a shelf.

45
00:02:24.750 --> 00:02:27.652
"Seeing that gum earlier made me want some.

46
00:02:28.448 --> 00:02:29.469
I think I'll buy some now."

47
00:02:30.190 --> 00:02:32.352
He grabbed a pack of cherry gum from the shelf.

48
00:02:35.454 --> 00:02:37.877
Henry and Cole waited for the other customer to finish.

49
00:02:38.817 --> 00:02:40.479
Then they stepped up to the counter again.

50
00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:42.981
Cole set down his pack of cherry gum.

51
00:02:43.001 --> 00:02:45.724
"Do you need anything else, boys?"

52
00:02:46.184 --> 00:02:48.226
Anna's mom asked as she rang up the sale.

53
00:02:49.227 --> 00:02:50.548
Cole handed over a dollar.

54
00:02:50.568 --> 00:02:51.789
"No, thanks."

55
00:02:53.210 --> 00:02:58.357
Henry was staring at the gum, still thinking about what William had just told them about seeing Roger

56
00:02:58.397 --> 00:03:02.498
again. Something didn't seem quite right about Roger's story.

57
00:03:03.758 --> 00:03:05.539
Why did they keep seeing him everywhere?

58
00:03:05.559 --> 00:03:08.780
"Excuse me," Henry said to Anna's mom.

59
00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:11.080
"Is Anna's sister around?"

60
00:03:12.041 --> 00:03:16.442
If Roger had really seen Anna's sister on the beach, maybe she'd seen him too.

61
00:03:17.342 --> 00:03:20.783
Or maybe she'd seen something else suspicious while she was out jogging.

62
00:03:21.943 --> 00:03:23.404
Anna's mom looked surprised.

63
00:03:24.128 --> 00:03:25.109
"Do you mean Josie?"

64
00:03:25.549 --> 00:03:25.989
she said.

65
00:03:26.009 --> 00:03:28.150
"She's not here right now.

66
00:03:28.691 --> 00:03:31.292
She's spending the whole weekend with friends out of town."

67
00:03:31.312 --> 00:03:33.654
"Really?" Henry said.

68
00:03:33.674 --> 00:03:36.135
"Is that Anna's only sister?"

69
00:03:37.036 --> 00:03:38.016
Anna's mom laughed.

70
00:03:38.036 --> 00:03:43.679
"Yes. And trust me, two kids in one family is plenty!"

71
00:03:44.020 --> 00:03:44.840
she said with a wink.

72
00:03:44.860 --> 00:03:47.121
"Okay, thanks."

73
00:03:48.062 --> 00:03:51.164
Henry wandered toward the door along with Cole, still thinking hard.

74
00:03:52.532 --> 00:03:55.434
Had Roger lied about seeing "the Jones girl" on the beach?

75
00:03:55.954 --> 00:03:57.275
Or was something else going on?

76
00:03:58.275 --> 00:04:00.937
He kept thinking as he and Cole left the general store.

77
00:04:00.957 --> 00:04:04.739
"We'd better find the others," Cole said.

78
00:04:04.759 --> 00:04:08.061
"Uh-huh." Henry didn't say anything else.

79
00:04:11.743 --> 00:04:14.724
He just kept thinking as he followed Cole across the street.

80
00:04:16.145 --> 00:04:21.108
He thought about everything that had happened so far, and everything everyone had said all day.

81
00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:23.181
Someone was lying.

82
00:04:23.861 --> 00:04:30.383
And Henry was starting to figure out who it might be Cole and Henry found the others standing

83
00:04:30.403 --> 00:04:32.124
at the edge of a small but pretty park.

84
00:04:32.144 --> 00:04:34.825
"We've been looking all over for you!"

85
00:04:35.165 --> 00:04:36.746
Maggie cried when she spotted them.

86
00:04:36.766 --> 00:04:39.107
"Yeah," Luke added.

87
00:04:39.127 --> 00:04:41.388
"We think we know where the next booty is hidden."

88
00:04:42.348 --> 00:04:43.609
Maggie nodded and pointed.

89
00:04:43.629 --> 00:04:46.870
"We're pretty sure it's in the old bandstand over there."

90
00:04:46.890 --> 00:04:49.051
"What are we waiting for?"

91
00:04:49.371 --> 00:04:50.191
Cole exclaimed.

92
00:04:50.211 --> 00:04:51.392
"Let's go!"

93
00:04:52.372 --> 00:04:54.874
"Wait," Henry spoke up before they could rush off.

94
00:04:55.755 --> 00:04:57.977
"First I need to ask Luke something.

95
00:04:59.098 --> 00:05:03.161
Remember when you and Nathan found the treasure in the tide pool and were waiting for the rest

96
00:05:03.201 --> 00:05:03.422
of us?"

97
00:05:03.442 --> 00:05:05.864
"Yeah," Luke said.

98
00:05:05.884 --> 00:05:11.388
"So?" "So exactly when did William get there?"

99
00:05:11.669 --> 00:05:12.389
Henry asked.

100
00:05:13.450 --> 00:05:14.311
William frowned.

101
00:05:14.331 --> 00:05:17.313
"I just told you guys I didn't take those tickets!"

102
00:05:17.594 --> 00:05:18.114
he cried.

103
00:05:18.134 --> 00:05:19.836
"I thought you believed me!"

104
00:05:20.896 --> 00:05:23.978
"Don't worry, I do believe you," Henry assured him.

105
00:05:24.719 --> 00:05:26.000
He continued to look at Luke.

106
00:05:26.020 --> 00:05:29.002
"Well?" Luke shrugged.

107
00:05:29.022 --> 00:05:33.545
"Actually, William was already there when Nathan and I found the tide pool."

108
00:05:34.486 --> 00:05:35.327
Nathan nodded.

109
00:05:35.347 --> 00:05:38.709
"Yeah." "Do you have a theory, Henry?"

110
00:05:38.969 --> 00:05:39.750
Maggie demanded.

111
00:05:39.770 --> 00:05:42.332
"Did William steal those tickets?

112
00:05:42.772 --> 00:05:44.053
Or was it Nathan and Luke?"

113
00:05:45.134 --> 00:05:48.056
"No, it wasn't any of them," Henry replied.

114
00:05:51.722 --> 00:05:52.510
"It was Anna."
